{
  "id": "fluency-l7-the-formula",
  "course": "quadratics",
  "lesson": "l7-the-formula",
  "title": "Fluency: the quadratic formula",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 15,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "discriminant",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "work out the part under the root",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [1, 5] },
        "b": { "int": [-9, 9] },
        "c": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "bb": "b^2", "fac": "4*a*c", "d": "b^2 - 4*a*c" },
      "where": ["gcd(a, abs(b), abs(c)) == 1"],
      "prompt": "For ${poly(v; a, b, c)} = 0$, what is $b^2 - 4ac$?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{d}", "tol": { "abs": 0 } },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "sign-of-4ac", "value": "{bb + fac}", "line": "Check the sign: $c = {c}$, so $4ac = {fac}$ and $b^2 - 4ac = {bb} - {fac:()}$." },
        { "id": "dropped-four", "value": "{bb - a*c}", "line": "You left out the 4: the part under the root is $b^2 - 4ac$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Here $a = {a}$, $b = {b}$ and $c = {c}$.",
        "$b^2 = {bb}$ and $4ac = 4 \\times {a} \\times {c:()} = {fac}$.",
        "So $b^2 - 4ac = {bb} - {fac:()} = {d}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "rational-roots",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "use the formula for fraction roots",
      "vars": {
        "p": { "int": [2, 4] },
        "q": { "int": [-7, 7], "not": [0] },
        "s": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] }
      },
      "let": {
        "a": "p", "b": "-(p*s + q)", "c": "q*s", "nb": "p*s + q", "a2": "2*p",
        "d": "(p*s + q)^2 - 4*p*q*s", "sd": "sqrt((p*s + q)^2 - 4*p*q*s)",
        "lo": "(p*s + q - sd)/(2*p)", "hi": "(p*s + q + sd)/(2*p)",
        "slo": "(-(p*s + q) - sd)/(2*p)", "shi": "(-(p*s + q) + sd)/(2*p)",
        "hlo": "p*s + q - sd/(2*p)", "hhi": "p*s + q + sd/(2*p)"
      },
      "where": ["gcd(p, abs(q)) == 1", "p*s + q != 0"],
      "prompt": "Solve ${poly(v; a, b, c)} = 0$ with the formula. Give both roots, as fractions or decimals.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answers": ["{lo}", "{hi}"], "unordered": true, "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "accept": "${lo:frac}$ and ${hi:frac}$, or decimals within 0.005" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "b-for-minus-b", "value": "{slo:dp6}, {shi:dp6}", "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "line": "The top starts with $-b$, which is ${nb}$ here, not ${b}$." },
        { "id": "halved-root-only", "value": "{hlo:dp6}, {hhi:dp6}", "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "line": "The whole top, $-b \\pm \\sqrt{{b^2 - 4ac}}$, goes over $2a$, not the square root alone." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Here $b^2 - 4ac = {d}$, and $\\sqrt{{{d}}} = {sd}$.",
        "So ${v} = \\frac{{{nb} \\pm {sd}}}{{{a2}}}$, which gives ${lo:frac}$ or ${hi:frac}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decimal-roots",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "use the formula to 2 decimal places",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [1, 3] },
        "b": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "c": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] }
      },
      "let": {
        "d": "b^2 - 4*a*c", "nb": "-b", "a2": "2*a",
        "lo": "(-b - sqrt(abs(d)))/(2*a)", "hi": "(-b + sqrt(abs(d)))/(2*a)",
        "slo": "(b - sqrt(abs(d)))/(2*a)", "shi": "(b + sqrt(abs(d)))/(2*a)",
        "hlo": "-b - sqrt(abs(d))/(2*a)", "hhi": "-b + sqrt(abs(d))/(2*a)"
      },
      "where": ["gcd(a, abs(b), abs(c)) == 1", "d > 0", "floor(sqrt(abs(d)))^2 != d"],
      "prompt": "Solve ${poly(v; a, b, c)} = 0$ with the formula. Give both roots to 2 decimal places.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answers": ["{lo}", "{hi}"], "unordered": true, "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "accept": "${lo:dp2}$ and ${hi:dp2}$" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "b-for-minus-b", "value": "{slo:dp6}, {shi:dp6}", "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "line": "The top starts with $-b$, which is ${nb}$ here, not ${b}$." },
        { "id": "halved-root-only", "value": "{hlo:dp6}, {hhi:dp6}", "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "line": "The whole top, $-b \\pm \\sqrt{{b^2 - 4ac}}$, goes over $2a$, not the square root alone." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Here $b^2 - 4ac = {d}$.",
        "So ${v} = \\frac{{{nb} \\pm \\sqrt{{{d}}}}}{{{a2}}}$.",
        "The roots are ${lo:dp2}$ and ${hi:dp2}$ to 2 decimal places."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "exact-roots",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "use the formula for exact surd roots",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [1, 3] },
        "b": { "pick": [-9, -7, -5, -3, -1, 1, 3, 5, 7, 9] },
        "c": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "d": "b^2 - 4*a*c", "nb": "-b", "a2": "2*a" },
      "where": ["gcd(a, abs(b), abs(c)) == 1", "d > 0", "floor(sqrt(abs(d)))^2 != d", "d % 9 != 0", "d % 25 != 0", "d % 49 != 0"],
      "prompt": "Solve ${poly(v; a, b, c)} = 0$ with the formula. Give both roots exactly, as surds.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answers": ["\\frac{{{nb}+\\sqrt{{{d}}}}}{{{a2}}}", "\\frac{{{nb}-\\sqrt{{{d}}}}}{{{a2}}}"], "unordered": true },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "b-for-minus-b", "tex": "\\frac{{{b}+\\sqrt{{{d}}}}}{{{a2}}}, \\frac{{{b}-\\sqrt{{{d}}}}}{{{a2}}}", "line": "The top starts with $-b$, which is ${nb}$ here, not ${b}$." },
        { "id": "over-a", "tex": "\\frac{{{nb}+\\sqrt{{{d}}}}}{{{a}}}, \\frac{{{nb}-\\sqrt{{{d}}}}}{{{a}}}", "line": "The bottom of the formula is $2a = {a2}$, not $a$.", "when": "a > 1" }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Here $a = {a}$, $b = {b}$ and $c = {c}$, so $b^2 - 4ac = {d}$, which is not a square.",
        "So ${v} = \\frac{{{nb} \\pm \\sqrt{{{d}}}}}{{{a2}}}$, two exact roots."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
